# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
/msis

# Native hook DLL (msi-simplica.dll) build artifacts. The DLL is produced by `just build-hooks`
# (and staged into templates/<arch>/); only the C++ source under native/ is tracked.
native/**/bin/
native/**/obj/

bootstrap/dist/

# Generated installer files
*.msi
*.wxs
*.wixpdb

# ...except the inspection fixture and its sources, which are test data rather than build
# output. fixture.msi is a 32 kB package carrying the four shapes internal/msiread has to handle
# and no released package contains: a merge module's contribution, a level-zero feature, a
# subdirectory named SourceDir, and a custom action in the ADMIN sequence that inspection must
# never run. Committing it is what lets those tests run in a clean checkout with no WiX
# toolchain, and the .wxs sources are what make it rebuildable.
#
# These exceptions must stay BELOW the patterns above: the last matching rule wins.
# Rebuild: see internal/msiread/testdata/README.md
!internal/msiread/testdata/*.msi
!internal/msiread/testdata/*.wxs

# The same for the bundle fixture. fixture.exe is a real Burn bundle whose engine code sections
# are zeroed after the build, so it packs to ~12 kB while still carrying the two things the
# reader parses: a genuine .wixburn section and the cabinets appended behind it.
# Rebuild: see internal/burnread/testdata/README.md
!internal/burnread/testdata/*.exe
!internal/burnread/testdata/*.wxs

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Code coverage profiles and other test artifacts
*.out
coverage.*
*.coverprofile
profile.cov
msis-coverage.xml
msis-junit.xml
msis-test.log

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# env file
.env

# Editor/IDE
# .idea/
# .vscode/

# A built SBOM index. It is derived from the CycloneDX corpus and rebuilt from scratch every
# time (#29 D12: the documents are authoritative), so a committed copy could only ever be a
# stale second answer.
*.db

# The sbom-index binary, when it is built rather than `go run`. Named rather than covered by a
# broad rule, because the directory is a module of its own and `go build` there drops the
# executable beside the source.
/tools/sbom-index/sbom-index
/tools/sbom-index/sbom-index.exe
